### Bitcoin Stamps

Bitcoin Stamps are immutable digital artifacts stored in Bitcoin's UTXO set, ensuring permanent on-chain storage.

**Documentation & Tools:**
- [Bitcoin Stamps Documentation](https://bitcoinstamps.xyz/en/) - Official protocol documentation and guides
- [Stamps Transaction Builder](https://github.com/btc-stamps/tx-builder) - TypeScript/JavaScript library for building stamp transactions

**Stampchain Explorer Ecosystem:**
- [Explorer Website](https://github.com/stampchain-io/BTCStampsExplorer) - Main explorer repository (Deno/Fresh)
- [Database Schema](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stampchain-io/btc_stamps/refs/heads/dev/indexer/table_schema.sql) - Complete SQL schema reference
- [Explorer API Documentation](https://stampchain.io/docs#/) - REST API for stamps, collections, and market data
- [Indexer Repository](https://github.com/stampchain-io/btc_stamps) - Python-based indexer implementation

**Key Concepts:**
- **UTXO-based storage**: Unlike Ordinals, stamps use UTXO data for permanence
- **SRC-20**: Fungible token standard on Bitcoin Stamps
- **SRC-721**: NFT collections on Bitcoin Stamps
- **OLGA format**: Optimized encoding reducing transaction size by 50%

**API Endpoints (Stampchain):**
```
GET /stamps - List all stamps
GET /stamp/{id} - Get stamp details
GET /address/{address}/stamps - Get stamps by address
GET /collection/{slug} - Get collection info
GET /src20/tokens - List SRC-20 tokens
GET /src20/balance/{address} - Get SRC-20 balances
```

