### Ordinals

Ordinals inscribe arbitrary data into the witness data of Bitcoin transactions, creating digital artifacts tied to specific satoshis.

#### API Provider Comparison (Free/Trial Tiers)

| Provider | RPS (Calls/Sec) | Calls/Day | Calls/Month | Status |
|----------|----------------|-----------|-------------|---------|
| **Xverse** | ~1.6 (100/min) | N/A | 100,000 total | 10-Day Free Trial |
| **UniSat** | 5 | 2,000 | 60,000 | Ongoing Free Tier ✓ |
| **Magic Eden** | ~8 (500/min) | N/A | Uncapped | Public Dev Access |
| **ordinals.com** | ~1-5 (est.) | Uncapped | Uncapped | Open Source/Self-hosted |
| **OrdiScan** | ~1.6 (100/min) | N/A | 1,000 | Ongoing Free Tier |
| **OrdinalsBot** | 0.2 (2/10s) | N/A | Unspecified | Highly Restricted |
| **OrdinalsWallet** | ~1-2 (est.) | N/A | N/A | Standard Web Limits |

**Provider Selection Guide:**

- **Xverse**: Best for short-term development (10-day trial, 100K calls). Converts to $59/month after trial.
- **UniSat**: Best "truly free" option for ongoing development (2,000 calls/day resets daily)
- **Magic Eden**: Highest throughput (8 RPS) for marketplace data (listings, sales, floor prices)
- **OrdiScan**: Proof-of-concept only (1,000 calls/month exhausts quickly)
- **ordinals.com**: Self-hosted option with no rate limits (requires infrastructure)

---

#### UniSat

**Documentation:**
- [UniSat API Documentation](https://unisat.io/open-api) - Overview, authentication, and usage guides
- [UniSat API Reference](https://open-api.unisat.io/) - Complete endpoint reference with examples

**Rate Limits:**
- 5 requests per second (RPS)
- 2,000 requests per day (resets daily)
- 60,000 requests per month
- Free tier (no credit card required)

**Key Endpoints:**
```
GET /v1/indexer/address/{address}/inscription-data - Get inscriptions by address
GET /v1/indexer/inscription/info/{inscriptionId} - Get inscription details
GET /v1/indexer/inscription/content/{inscriptionId} - Get inscription content
GET /v1/indexer/brc20/list - List BRC-20 tokens
GET /v1/indexer/brc20/{ticker}/holders - Get BRC-20 holders
```

**Use Cases:**
- Fetching user's inscription collection
- Displaying inscription metadata and content
- BRC-20 token balances and transfers
- Runes protocol data

